I go towards a vegetable stall.
It is very crowded there.
There are fresh, red tomatoes in the shop.
I ask the shopkeeper.
"Brother, what is the price of tomatoes?"
The shopkeeper takes a tomato in his hand.
He tells me, "Forty rupees a kilo, Madam."
The tomatoes are indeed very nice.
I say to him, "Give me half a kilo of tomatoes."
He puts tomatoes in the weighing scale.
Then he weighs them.
I open my cloth bag.
He puts those tomatoes into my bag.
I ask him, "How much is it?"
He says, "Only twenty rupees."
I take out a twenty-rupee note from my wallet.
I give that note to him.
He takes the money and says, "Thank you, Madam."
